#s
disablemonitor
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Disables the VXIbus monitor, which monitors
the status of the VXIbus in the system.
 
#s
enablemonitor [<controller>]
  <controller> logical address of extended
               controller or embedded controller
               to monitor or -2
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Enables the VXIbus monitor, which monitors
the status of the VXIbus in the system
for the specified controller. If no controller
field is specified, the monitoring for the last
controller being monitored is enabled.
(-2 = OR of all controllers)

#s
lpeek <address>,<width>
  <address> address on the local device
   <width>  1 = byte,2 = word,4 = longword 
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Reads a single byte, word, or longword from
the specified address on the local VXI device.

#s
lpoke <address>,<width>,<value>
 <address>  address on the local device
   <width>  1 = byte,2 = word,4 = longword 
   <value>  value to write
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Writes a single byte, word, or longword to
the specified address on the local VXI device.

#s
set <la> or <devname>
  Note: The single parameter with set command can 
        be <la> which is the logical address of the
        device, or <devname> which is the name
        of the device in "". Partial names
        will work for the <devname> parameter.
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Invokes device level calls.  The command line
prompt changes to the device name. At this
stage you no longer need to specify <la> in
the VIC Word Serial and some Auxiliary commands.

#s
pparms [<accessparms>]
  <accessparms> (same as in vxiin)
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Sets the specified access parameters.
These access parameters are used in peek
and poke VIC commands.  If no parameter 
is specified, it displays the current
access parameters.
 
#s
pwidth [<width>]
  <width> 1 = byte,2 = word,4 = longword
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Sets the specified width.
This width is used in peek and poke VIC or
VICTEXT commands. If no parameter is
specified, it displays the current width.
 
#s
peek <address>
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Reads a single byte, word, or longword (depending
upon the width set by the pwidth VIC command) from
the specified address (in the address space with 
access parameters set by the pparms VIC command).

#s
poke <address>,<value>
#t
Auxiliary Command
#p
Writes a single byte, word, or longword
(depending upon the width set by the
pwidth VIC command) to the specified
address (in the address space with
access parameters set by the pparms
VIC command).

